        </nav>

        <article class="prose max-w-none">
          <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-ink mb-4 dark:text-on-primary">Pakistan Token Tax Guide: Vehicle & Property Token Tax Rates</h1>
          <p class="text-lg text-body dark:text-muted">Last updated: August 2026 | Verified Provincial Excise Schedules | 9 min read</p>

          <div class="mt-8 space-y-6 text-body dark:text-muted leading-relaxed">
            <p>Token tax in Pakistan is an annual fee collected by provincial Excise and Taxation Departments from vehicle owners under provincial motor vehicle acts. Active taxpayer filers enjoy discounts up to 50% on token withholding taxes.</p>

            <div class="my-6 p-6 rounded-2xl border border-primary/30 bg-primary/5 dark:border-primary/20 dark:bg-primary/5 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-4">
              <div>
                <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">Calculate Pakistan Token Tax & Vehicle Tax</h3>
                <p class="text-sm text-body dark:text-muted mt-1">Select your province (Punjab, Sindh, ICT), engine capacity (CC), and filer status for instant estimates.</p>
              </div>
              <a href="/countries/pakistan/property-tax/token-tax-calculator" class="btn btn-primary text-sm font-semibold shrink-0 px-5 py-2.5">
                Launch Token Tax Calculator →
              </a>
            </div>


            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">Property Token Tax (Annual Property Tax)</h2>
            <p>Property token tax is the annual Urban Immovable Property Tax (UIPT) levied by provincial excise and taxation departments. Rates differ by province:</p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
              <li><strong>Punjab:</strong> 5% of Annual Rental Value (ARV). Punjab is transitioning from ARV-based assessment to capital value based on DC rates.</li>
              <li><strong>Sindh:</strong> 25% of ARV under the Sindh UIPT Act 1958. Because Sindh's valuation tables set ARV low, the actual payable amount is often lower than the headline rate implies.</li>
              <li><strong>KPK:</strong> Category-based tax under KP UIPT Act 2013. Commercial properties pay higher rates than residential.</li>
              <li><strong>Islamabad (ICT):</strong> Collected by CDA on a slab-based schedule.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>Property token tax bills are typically sent as PT-10 challans. You can view and download them online using your CNIC and Property Tax Number, then pay via the provincial e-payment portal.</p>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">Vehicle Transfer Fees</h2>
            <p>When you buy or sell a vehicle, you pay a transfer fee to update ownership records with the Excise Department. Transfer fees vary by province and vehicle type:</p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
              <li><strong>Registration fee:</strong> One-time fee for new registrations, usually 1% to 5% of vehicle invoice value depending on engine size.</li>
              <li><strong>Transfer fee:</strong> Paid by the buyer during ownership transfer. Typical amounts range from PKR 200 to PKR 4,000 based on vehicle class.</li>
              <li><strong>Smart card fee:</strong> Additional cost for plastic smart card registration in many provinces.</li>
              <li><strong>Map or naqsha penalty:</strong> Some provinces charge a penalty if the property map is not available at the sub-registrar (Punjab: 2% of value).</li>
            </ul>
            <p>The seller must clear all outstanding token tax before the transfer can be processed. Both buyer and seller need CNIC copies and the original registration book.</p>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">How to Pay Token Tax Online</h2>
            <p>Most provinces have digitized their token tax payment systems. Here is how to pay online:</p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
              <li><strong>Punjab:</strong> Use the ePay Punjab app or visit epay.punjab.gov.pk. Enter your vehicle registration number or CNIC, download the PT-10 challan, and pay via banking app, ATM, JazzCash, or Easypaisa.</li>
              <li><strong>Sindh:</strong> Visit excise.gos.pk or download the e-Payment GOS app. Generate a PSID and pay through internet banking, mobile banking, or a bank counter.</li>
              <li><strong>KPK:</strong> Check dues on the KP Excise portal and pay at designated bank branches or online.</li>
              <li><strong>Islamabad:</strong> Pay through the MTMIS portal or FBR's online channels using your vehicle registration number.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>Always keep your payment receipt or counterfoil as proof of payment. Traffic police can impose fines if you cannot show valid token tax status during a checkpoint stop.</p>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">Conclusion</h2>
            <p>Token tax is a recurring ownership cost that every vehicle and property owner in Pakistan must manage. By paying before the 31 August early-payment deadline, maintaining your FBR filer status, and using provincial online portals, you can reduce your expenses and avoid penalties. Use our <a href="/countries/pakistan/vehicle-tax/vehicle-tax-calculator">token tax calculator</a> to estimate your annual dues instantly.</p>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">What is vehicle token tax in Pakistan?</h3>
            <p>Vehicle token tax is an annual fee collected by provincial Excise and Taxation Departments to renew your vehicle's legal right to operate on public roads. It is governed under the Motor Vehicle Ordinance, 1965.</p>

            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">Do filers pay less token tax than non-filers?</h3>
            <p>Yes. In many provinces, filers pay half the non-filer rate on withholding tax. A 1800cc vehicle owner in KPK may pay PKR 6,000 as a filer versus PKR 12,000 as a non-filer.</p>

            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">How do I pay token tax online in Punjab?</h3>
            <p>Use the ePay Punjab app or epay.punjab.gov.pk. Enter your vehicle registration number to download the PT-10 challan, then pay via banking app, ATM, or mobile wallet using the generated PSID.</p>

            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">What is the early-payment rebate for token tax?</h3>
            <p>Punjab and several other provinces offer a 10% discount if you pay the full annual token tax by 31 August. Paying late can trigger escalating penalties.</p>

            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">Is there lifetime token tax for vehicles?</h3>
            <p>Yes. Punjab and Sindh offer lifetime token tax options for small vehicles, such as cars up to 1000cc and motorcycles. This is a one-time payment that eliminates annual token tax for the vehicle's life.</p>

            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">What is the difference between token tax and registration fee?</h3>
            <p>Token tax is an annual renewal fee for keeping your vehicle on the road. Registration fee is a one-time payment made when registering a new vehicle for the first time.</p>

            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">What happens if I do not pay token tax on time?</h3>
            <p>Late payment attracts penalties and may block vehicle transfer or resale. In Punjab, unpaid token tax can result in a penalty of up to the full tax amount plus additional late fees. Traffic police can also fine or impound vehicles without valid tokens.</p>
          </div>

